### Case: wrong-issuer — a correctly signed, unexpired token from a DIFFERENT Okta
### authorization server. Expect 401.
###
### This is the case that proves the token is specific to THIS API rather than
### merely "a valid token from somewhere". It is the counterpart to solution 01's
### wrong-client-secret case: without it you have demonstrated that signatures are
### checked, not that the right issuer is required.
GET {{GATEWAY}}/posts
authorization: Bearer {{OTHER_ISSUER_TOKEN}}
accept: application/json
